{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class div25_v5 {\n    private static char[] data;\n    private static int size;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        data = br.readLine().toCharArray();\n        size = data.length;\n        int sum = 0;\n\n        if (size == 1) {\n            char c = data[0];\n            if (c == 'X' || c == '_' || (c == '0')) {\n                sum = 1;\n            }\n        } else {\n            sum += ways(2, 5);\n            sum += ways(5, 0);\n            sum += ways(7, 5);\n            sum += ways(0, 0);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(sum);\n    }\n\n    private static int ways(int a, int b) {\n        int x = -1;\n\n        if (data[size - 2] == 'X') {\n            x = a;\n        } else if (data[size - 2] != '_') {\n            if (toNum(size - 2) != a) return 0;\n        }\n\n        if (data[size - 1] == 'X') {\n            if (x != -1 && b != x) return 0;\n            else x = b;\n        } else if (data[size - 1] != '_') {\n            if (toNum(size - 1) != b) return 0;\n        }\n\n        long ways = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < size - 2; i++) {\n            if (i == 0) {\n                if (data[i] == 'X' && x == 0) return 0;\n                if (toNum(0) == 0) return 0;\n            }\n\n            if (data[i] == '_') {\n                ways *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            } else if (data[i] == 'X') {\n                if (x != -1) continue;\n                x = 10;\n                ways *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return (int) ways;\n    }\n\n    private static int toNum(int idx) {\n        char c = data[idx];\n        return (c >= '0' && c <= '9') ? c - '0' : -1;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class div25_v5 {\n    private static char[] data;\n    private static int size;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        data = br.readLine().toCharArray();\n        size = data.length;\n        long sum = 0;\n\n        // For divisibility by 25, last two digits must be: 00, 25, 50, or 75\n        int[][] lastTwo = {{0,0}, {2,5}, {5,0}, {7,5}};\n\n        for (int[] pair : lastTwo) {\n            sum += countValid(pair[0], pair[1]);\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(sum);\n    }\n\n    private static long countValid(int tens, int ones) {\n        // Check if last two digits can be tens and ones\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n            int pos = size - 2 + i;\n            if (pos < 0) continue;\n            char c = data[pos];\n            int target = (i == 0) ? tens : ones;\n            \n            if (c == 'X') {\n                // X must match target, but also must be consistent across all X positions\n                // We'll handle consistency later in the main loop\n            } else if (c == '_') {\n                // Can be replaced with target\n            } else {\n                // Must be a digit\n                int digit = c - '0';\n                if (digit != target) {\n                    return 0;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Count ways to assign digits to X and _ positions\n        long ways = 1;\n        int[] xDigit = new int[1]; // -1 means not determined yet, otherwise the digit X must be\n        xDigit[0] = -1;\n\n        // First pass: determine what X must be if it appears in last two positions\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) {\n            int pos = size - 2 + i;\n            if (pos < 0) continue;\n            if (data[pos] == 'X') {\n                int target = (i == 0) ? tens : ones;\n                if (xDigit[0] == -1) {\n                    xDigit[0] = target;\n                } else if (xDigit[0] != target) {\n                    return 0; // Inconsistent X requirements\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Second pass: count ways for each position\n        for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n            char c = data[i];\n            \n            if (c == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    // First digit cannot be 0\n                    ways *= 9; // digits 1-9\n                } else {\n                    ways *= 10; // digits 0-9\n                }\n            } else if (c == 'X') {\n                if (xDigit[0] == -1) {\n                    // X is not constrained yet, we need to count all possibilities\n                    if (i == 0) {\n                        // First digit: 1-9\n                        ways *= 9;\n                    } else {\n                        ways *= 10;\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    // X is constrained, no additional choices\n                    // But check if it violates leading zero rule\n                    if (i == 0 && xDigit[0] == 0) {\n                        return 0;\n                    }\n                }\n            } else {\n                // Fixed digit\n                if (i == 0 && c == '0') {\n                    return 0; // Leading zero not allowed (except for single \"0\")\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Additional check: if X is constrained, verify no leading zero\n        if (xDigit[0] == 0) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n                if (data[i] == 'X' && i == 0) {\n                    return 0;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        return ways;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.152555099310121e-07, -6.09140915912576e-05, -3.576272320060525e-06, 0.0, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -2.47952248173533e-05, -2.861018856492592e-06, -9.298280929215252e-06, -3.981510963058099e-05, -1.0609570381348021e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.814624506048858e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -0.07098910957574844, 0.0, -4.768370